text.section:
The Commission shall charge a fee:

Of $1,800 for investigating an application for authority to establish a branch, if the branch is to be located within the Commonwealth;


As prescribed by the Commission for investigating an application for authority to establish a branch if the branch is to be located outside the Commonwealth;


Of $1,000 for investigating an application for authority to change the location of an existing main office or branch office;


Of $10,000 for investigating an application for a certificate of authority in the case of a state association;


As prescribed by the Commission for investigating an application for a certificate of authority in the case of a foreign savings institution;


Of $7,500 for investigating an application for merger or consolidation;


Of $2,000 for investigating an application for authority to exercise trust powers if such powers are to be exercised through a trust department;


Of $10,000 for investigating an application for authority to exercise trust powers if such powers are to be exercised through a trust affiliate or subsidiary;


Of $5,000 for investigating an application to convert from a state association to a state savings bank pursuant to subsection B of § 6.2-1143 or from a state bank to a state savings bank pursuant to § 6.2-829; and


Of $10,000 for investigating an application for a conversion other than a conversion from a state association or state bank to a state savings bank as provided in subdivision 9.
